Subject: nrUE: assume dmrs-AdditionalPosition pos2 on DCI format 0_0 grants

TS 38.214 Section 6.2.2 has the UE assume dmrs-AdditionalPosition = pos2 for a
PUSCH scheduled by DCI format 0_0, whatever dmrs-UplinkForPUSCH-MappingTypeA
says. The nrUE instead applied the dedicated value as soon as a pusch-Config
existed, for every DCI format.

That is invisible while the dedicated value is pos2 -- the default -- and a hard
attach failure otherwise. The gNB's fallback scheduler builds msg5's UL grant
with the common DMRS information (pos2, three DMRS symbols on a 14-symbol type-A
allocation); the UE, having just applied the master cell group from RRCSetup,
transmits the dedicated pattern (pos1 -> two DMRS symbols). msg5 never decodes,
RLC hits max retransmissions, RRC releases, and the UE loops through random
access forever: "Received indication that RLC reached max retransmissions"
followed by repeated "RAR reception failed".

Only affects a cell configured with cell_cfg.pusch.dmrs_additional_position
set to 1; a cell at the pos2 default behaves identically either way.

Origin: DeepSig, 2026-08-23. Applies to
github.com/duranta-project/openairinterface5g @ develop, which does not have the
guard. Upstream OAI status not verified. OAI is under the Collaborative
Standards Software License v1.0 (LicenseRef-CSSL-1.0, text in LICENSES/);
nr_ue_scheduler.c carries that identifier itself. OAI-PL-v1.1 is deprecated
upstream. This file is a modification to OAI, not to any OCUDU component.

--- a/openair2/LAYER2/NR_MAC_UE/nr_ue_scheduler.c
+++ b/openair2/LAYER2/NR_MAC_UE/nr_ue_scheduler.c
@@ -923,7 +923,10 @@
     /* HARQ_PROCESS_NUMBER */
     pusch_config_pdu->pusch_data.harq_process_id = pid;
 
-    if (NR_DMRS_ulconfig != NULL)
+    // TS 38.214 6.2.2: a PUSCH scheduled by DCI format 0_0 uses the default
+    // dmrs-AdditionalPosition (pos2, set above), not the dedicated value, which
+    // is what the gNB's fallback scheduler assumes for msg5.
+    if (NR_DMRS_ulconfig != NULL && dci_format != NR_UL_DCI_FORMAT_0_0)
       add_pos = (NR_DMRS_ulconfig->dmrs_AdditionalPosition == NULL) ? 2 : *NR_DMRS_ulconfig->dmrs_AdditionalPosition;
 
     /* DMRS */
